    /* ===== COMIC-STYLE SPEECH BUBBLES =====
       Each bubble is a DOM element layered over the 3D scene, positioned
       by projecting the speaker figure's head world-coord to screen-coord
       every animation frame. White fill + black outline + downward tail
       so it reads instantly as a comic-strip speech balloon. User wanted
       crew talking to each other visibly: "they need to talk like how
       you see in comics. I can't tell they are communicating." */
    .pad-speech-layer {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      pointer-events: none;
      z-index: 5;            /* above the canvas, below the camera buttons */
    }
    /* Voice debug panel — diagnostic overlay for SpeechSynthesis.
